{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Waters read the proclamation aloud. \par
\par
Tyler Swanson, Chair of WCPSS, shared that on behalf of the WCPSS board, he and Vice Chair Hershey want to thank the board for their partnership with WCPSS. He shared that the five-year commitment shows WCPSS's commitment to the partnership with the Wake County Board of Commissioners. He shared that the State Legislator has failed to invest in public schools and has diverted funds from public schools, and that the Wake County Board of Commissioners has saved Wake County Public Schools when they needed it the most. He thanked the board for putting educators first and students first. He shared that this shows across the nation and the state what strong collaboration looks like between the Board of Education and the Board of Commissioners. He shared that this is a model that he is proud that they all will stand in, and that's the rich history shared that he is confident that they will all continue to advocate for our students and teachers. He thanked the board for putting WCPSS first and center in their decisions because when we invest in our schools, we are investing in our communities, economy, and our workforce. He shared that he is looking at getting into good trouble together. \par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
